     3	description: SearchFn on Hono with the Memory adapter for dev and Postgres for prod.
     4	---
     5	
     6	This guide gets a Hono server indexing and searching in under 10 minutes. The same shape works on Bun, Deno, or Node.
     7	
     8	## 1. Install
     9	
    10	```bash
    11	npm install hono @searchfn/server @searchfn/adapter-memory
    12	```
    13	
    14	For production with Postgres:
    15	
    16	```bash
    17	npm install @searchfn/adapter-postgres
    18	```
    19	
    20	## 2. Mount SearchFn on Hono
    21	
    22	```typescript
    23	import { Hono } from "hono";
    24	import { createSearchFnServer } from "@searchfn/server";
    25	import { MemoryAdapter } from "@searchfn/adapter-memory";
    26	
    27	const sf = await createSearchFnServer({
    28	  adapter: new MemoryAdapter(),
    29	  basePath: "/searchfn",
    30	});
    31	
    32	await sf.adapter.initialize?.({
    33	  resources: [
    34	    { name: "articles", searchFields: ["title", "body"] },
    35	  ],
    36	});
    37	
    38	const app = new Hono();
    39	
    40	app.all("/searchfn/*", async (c) => {
    41	  const res = await sf.router.handle({
    42	    method: c.req.method,
    43	    url: c.req.url,
    44	    headers: c.req.raw.headers,
    45	    body: c.req.raw.body,
    46	  });
    47	  return new Response(res.body, { status: res.status, headers: res.headers });
    48	});
    49	
    50	export default app;
    51	```
    52	
    53	`@searchfn/server` exposes a generic `router` that adapts to any HTTP framework through small request/response shims. The example above is a 10-line shim; if you use `@superfunctions/http`'s Hono adapter, you can drop the shim entirely.
    54	
    55	## 3. Run
    56	
    57	```bash
    58	npx tsx --watch server.ts
    59	```
    60	
    61	Server listens on the default Hono port (3000).
    62	
