`import.meta.glob("../../../static/**/*", { query: "?raw", eager: true })` eagerly raw-imports every file in the SvelteKit `static/` directory as a UTF-8 string. `static/` is the conventional location for binary assets (favicon, images, fonts); any such file added later is decoded as text (corrupted bytes in the `source`/`byteLength` asset entries) or fails the build, and the eager import also inlines the full content of every static file into the server bundle. restrict the glob to text extensions (e.g. `["../../../static/**/*.txt", "../../../static/**/*.json"]`) or read asset metadata without `?raw` for binary types.

