`import.meta.glob("../../../static/**/*", { query: "?raw", eager: true })` eagerly imports every file under `static/` as a raw string. The `assetsDir` is `static` and is where real site assets (images, fonts, favicon) will be placed — every such asset will be read as a string and inlined into the server/SSR bundle in addition to being served from the static directory, bloating bundle size and memory per worker instance, and raw-importing binary files can produce corrupted entries. Restrict the glob to the text artifacts the provider actually needs (e.g. `../../../static/*.txt` or an `assetsManifest` convention) or filter by extension before creating asset entries.

```typescript
const bundledStatic = import.meta.glob("../../../static/*.{txt,json,md}", {
  query: "?raw",
  import: "default",
  eager: true,
}) as Record<string, string>;
```





