The layout server load returns the entire `source` object — the full DocsManifest (which retains every page's markdown body, as consumed by `createCompiledCache` via `page.body`) plus the complete search artifact — into layout data, which SvelteKit serializes into every SSR HTML response and hydration payload. Every route request transfers the whole site's content (and the search index, which is also fetched separately via `/search.json` by DocsSiteSearch) so page payload grows linearly with total documentation size, doubling the search data on the client. Return only the fields the layout actually renders (siteTitle, config.navigation/site, canonicalUrl, compatPreset) and keep manifest/searchArtifact server-only, accessed via the existing getCompiledDocsPage/createDocsSiteSearchRuntime helpers.

```typescript
export const load: LayoutServerLoad = async () => {
  const source = await loadDocsSiteSource();
  return {
    source: {
      siteRoot: source.siteRoot,
      siteTitle: source.siteTitle,
      canonicalUrl: source.canonicalUrl,
      compatPreset: source.compatPreset,
      config: {
        ...source.config,
        content: { ...source.config.content },
      },
      // manifest/searchArtifact fetched lazily where needed, not shipped to the client
      manifest: {} as DocsManifest,
      searchArtifact: undefined as unknown as DocsSearchArtifact,
    },
  };
};
```





